---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "10 June 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Swimly"
  description="How Swimly collects, uses, and protects your personal data on swimly.uk. Plain English, no legal maze."
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section class="relative pt-32 pb-16 sm:pt-40 overflow-hidden">
      <div class="dot-grid absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-[480px] pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl leading-tight text-[#0F2D2D] mt-5">Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-ink-mute">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
          This policy explains what personal data we collect through swimly.uk, why we collect it,
          and what your rights are. We have written it in plain English because that is how we
          would want it explained to us.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pb-20 sm:pb-28">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-12">

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">Who we are</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            Swimly is club management software for UK swimming clubs, operated from the United Kingdom.
            For anything related to your personal data, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:hello@swimly.uk" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline underline-offset-2">hello@swimly.uk</a>.
            For data collected through this website, Swimly is the data controller.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">What we collect and why</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-2">Waitlist signups</h3>
              <p>
                If you join the waitlist, we store your email address (and your club name and role
                if you choose to share them) so we can contact you about Swimly launch updates and
                the founding clubs programme. That is the only thing we use it for. The lawful basis
                is your consent, and you can withdraw it at any time by emailing us or using the
                unsubscribe link in any email we send.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-2">Contact form enquiries</h3>
              <p>
                If you use the contact form, we receive the details you enter: your name, email
                address, club name, role, and message. We use them to respond to your enquiry and
                for nothing else. The lawful basis is our legitimate interest in answering the
                people who write to us. The form is delivered to our inbox by FormSubmit, which
                acts as a processor for this purpose.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-2">Analytics</h3>
              <p>
                We use Google Analytics to understand which pages are useful, and only if you
                accept analytics cookies in the banner. If you decline, Google Analytics does not
                load and no analytics cookies are set. The lawful basis is your consent. See the
                cookies section below for how to change your choice.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-2">Club directory</h3>
              <p>
                Our <a href="/clubs/" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline underline-offset-2">club directory</a>
                lists UK swimming clubs using publicly available information such as club names,
                locations, and websites. It does not contain personal data about club members. If
                you represent a club and want your listing corrected or removed, email us and we
                will sort it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">Who we share data with</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            We never sell your data. We share it only with the service providers that make this
            website work: our hosting providers, FormSubmit (contact form delivery), and Google
            Analytics (analytics, only with your consent). Each acts under terms that restrict
            what they can do with it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">How long we keep it</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            Waitlist emails are kept until you unsubscribe or until launch communications are
            complete, after which the list is deleted. Contact enquiries are kept for as long as
            needed to deal with your enquiry and any follow-up, then deleted.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">Your rights</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Under UK GDPR you have the right to access the personal data we hold about you, to
            correct it, to have it deleted, to restrict or object to how we use it, and to receive
            a copy in a portable format. Email
            <a href="mailto:hello@swimly.uk" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline underline-offset-2">hello@swimly.uk</a>
            and we will respond within one month.
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            If you are unhappy with how we have handled your data, you can complain to the
            Information Commissioner's Office at
            <a href="https://ico.org.uk" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline underline-offset-2" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">ico.org.uk</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="cookies">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">Cookies</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mb-4">
            This site sets no cookies unless you accept them. If you accept analytics in the
            consent banner, Google Analytics sets its standard cookies to measure page visits.
            Your choice is stored in your browser so we do not ask you on every visit.
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mb-6">
            You can change your mind at any time:
          </p>
          <button
            id="reset-consent"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 rounded-xl border border-[#297373]/40 text-ink hover:border-[#297373]/70 hover:bg-surface transition-colors font-semibold min-h-12"
          >
            Reset cookie preferences
          </button>
          <p id="reset-consent-message" class="mt-3 text-sm text-mint-ink hidden">
            Done. Reload any page to choose again.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-4">Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
            If we change this policy we will update this page and the date at the top. If a change
            meaningfully affects how we use your data, we will tell you by email before it takes
            effect.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<script>
  const btn = document.getElementById("reset-consent");
  const msg = document.getElementById("reset-consent-message");
  btn?.addEventListener("click", () => {
    localStorage.removeItem("swimly-consent");
    msg?.classList.remove("hidden");
  });
</script>
